    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">As a Sensor Property: Sensitivity is the quotient of the change in a Result of Observation and the corresponding change in a value of an ObservableProperty being observed, under the defined Conditions.

       As an Actuator Property: Sensitivity is the quotient of the change in a command of Actuation and the corresponding change in a value of an ActuatableProperty being acted on, under the defined Conditions.</skos:definition>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">As a Sensor Property: Sensitivity is the quotient of the change in a Result of Observation and the corresponding change in a value of an ObservableProperty being observed, under the defined Conditions.

       As an Actuator Property: Sensitivity is the quotient of the change in a command of Actuation and the corresponding change in a value of an ActuatableProperty being acted on, under the defined Conditions.</rdfs:comment>
